     The design lesson to keep

     Tidal’s State does not mean the query model was wrong.

     It means:
     > “query by arc” was the core,
     > and later they realized patterns sometimes need more than time to decide what to emit.
     That is an extension, not a contradiction.

     ---

     My recommendation in one sentence

     For your Rust engine:
     1. build arc-only patterns first
     2. get whole/part, stack, cat, fast, slow correct
     3. only then consider whether you need stateful querying

